verdicts and reasons. Missing, incomplete or invalid assessments MUST remain absent,
without preventing the rest of the review from loading or defaulting to low risk.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 request to implement Warp's merge-risk assessment in Pully.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] shared-data-keeps-server-wire-models
The shared inbox, diff, review and AI models MUST retain the existing server field
names, nullable states and defaults as their Android callers move across modules.
Unknown optional server fields MUST NOT prevent parsing a supported response. The
models MUST NOT call GitHub or model providers. Source: `data-server-is-the-source`
and Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 decision to share the actual Pully implementation for iOS.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] shared-data-keeps-timestamp-meaning
An inbox row's valid ISO instant or numeric-offset timestamp MUST retain its epoch
millisecond value on both platforms. Missing or malformed timestamps and millisecond
overflow MUST remain unknown rather than become stale rows or a fabricated time.
The existing Android ISO_INSTANT handling of leap seconds, end-of-day midnight and
submillisecond rounding MUST be retained. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 same-app iOS
decision and the existing parser behavior used by inbox age and stale filtering.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] shared-data-retains-lite-file-state
A lite diff's files MUST retain `patchOmitted` and their blob identity. A later patch
MUST clear omission only when applied, and the existing identity-match policy MUST
reject conflicting known blob SHAs while retaining compatibility with servers that
omit a SHA. Source: `android/DESIGN.md` rules 51 and 52; architecture, The phone reads
the server's store; existing `data-lite-diffs` behavior shared for iOS on 21 Oct 2026.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] shared-data-keeps-critique-identity
Parsing a saved critique MUST retain its head SHA, variant and immutable revision.
Missing variant or revision MUST remain absent so legacy display data cannot become
authority to post an unidentified result. Source: `data-posts-selected-critique-revision`,
repository review 15 Oct 2026 finding 8; retained by the 21 Oct 2026 shared-code decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] shared-server-base-has-no-credentials
The configured server base MUST be an absolute HTTP(S) address without userinfo,
query, fragment, whitespace or ambiguous authority escapes. Invalid addresses MUST
fail without reflecting credentials in the error. Passwords and sessions MUST use
HTTPS except for localhost, 127.0.0.1 and 10.0.2.2 development hosts. Source:
`data-no-user-credentials`, Devin Review on PR 58, and the accepted 21 Oct 2026 iOS
client extraction and origin-confinement plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] source-cache-namespace-includes-authorization
Durable private cache namespaces MUST distinguish normalized server, eligible account
identity and configured Access authorization. Header names and order MUST be canonical;
session renewal for the same eligible owner MUST NOT change the namespace. Only an
opaque digest MAY leave namespace derivation; raw credentials MUST NOT be persisted or
logged. Invalid server configuration MUST produce no namespace. Source: the accepted
21 Oct iOS source-identity plan and its explicit account/server cache boundary.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-feedback-reports-the-actual-platform
Feedback MUST retain Android's existing report fields and note/history parsing. An
iOS report MUST name its actual app version, generic model and iOS version, omit the
Android version and SDK fields, and MUST NOT attach device identifiers, credentials
or analytics content. Source: server-feedback-kept-for-agents and Tavi's 21 Oct 2026
same-app iOS request with thin native metadata adapters.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] stored-tours-keep-the-existing-cache-policy
Both native hosts MUST use the same original TourResult parser, nonempty-stop check,
generated-time duplicate suppression and 200-tour cache policy. A missing file MUST
remain repairable; corrupt entries MUST become unavailable and removable. A native
cache failure MUST NOT hide the current server result, and revoked source handles
MUST NOT read, remember, write or delete another source's data. Source: existing
Android TourStore, data-tours-are-kept (CHANGELOG 0.28.0) and Tavi's accepted
21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse and private-cache ownership plan.
